==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Indo-European|dʰeh₁-|to put, place, set|lang=la}}. Cognates include Ancient Greek {{term|sc=polytonic|τίθημι|tr=tithēmi|lang=grc}}, Sanskrit {{term|sc=Deva|दधाति|tr=dádhāti|lang=sa}}, Old English {{term|don|dōn|lang=ang}} (English {{term|do}}).

===Verb===
{{la-verb|facio|faciō|facere|facere|feci|fēcī|factum|factum|pattern=irregular [[passive]]}}

# I [[do]]; I [[make]].
#: ''Quid ego '''feci'''?''
#:: ''What '''have''' I '''done'''?''
#: ''Latrocinium modo '''factum est'''.'' (''special usage''; passive perfect = took place)
#:: ''A robbery just '''took place'''.''

====Inflection====
* The verb has an irregular conjugation as for the [[passive voice]].
{{la-conj-3rd-IO-facio|f|11=f}}

